{
  "_note": [
    "Input to tools/build-vocab.mjs. NOT shipped content: the shipped content is",
    "data/vocab/*.json, which this file selects out of jmdict-eng-common.",
    "Each word is a lookup, not a translation. `q` matches a kanji or kana form",
    "exactly; `pos` disambiguates when a form has several entries (は is a",
    "particle and also a tooth); `reading` picks one kana form when JMdict lists",
    "several and the first is not the one a beginner should learn (four is よん,",
    "not し, in a counting drill). `senses` caps how many glosses are kept.",
    "A word that resolves to nothing is reported by name and the run fails, so a",
    "typo here can never become a silently shorter deck.",
    "`jmdict` pins one entry by id, and it is the only thing that tells 事 the",
    "noun from 琴 the zither when the query is こと: pickEntry takes the first",
    "entry whose queried form is common, and that is not always the one a",
    "chapter means.",
    "A group may ask for derived fields with `emit`: `misc` (the tracked JMdict",
    "tags), `spelling` (kana or kanji), `script` (hiragana, katakana or kanji),",
    "`shape` (the mimetic family, off the kana) and `register` (hon, hum, pol or",
    "plain, by precedence). Emission is per group and not per file, because a",
    "field exists for the exercise that answers against it, and a slice built",
    "before these fields existed emits the same bytes it emitted before.",
    "`situation` and `set` are authored labels passed through untouched. They",
    "are never a gloss: the chapter page says the labels are ours.",
    "`accept` asks for every reading a typed drill should mark right, per group",
    "or per word. Two shipped drills answer against it.",
    "`min_items`, `require_values` and `distinct_entries` are the assertions:",
    "a group that resolves short, a group missing one of the answers its drill",
    "needs, or two spellings that are one JMdict entry all fail the run."
  ],
